## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to translate a compliance feature into a concrete, time-bound cost-benefit analysis suitable for a beginner. It tests how assumptions drive ROI and how to articulate go/no-go criteria.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation basics for small features
- ROI calculation and break-even timing
- Risk penalties avoided and adoption uplift
- Simple, testable calculations and trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function breakEvenMonths(laborRatePerHr, weeks, engineers, monthlyOverhead, annualBenefit) {
  const upfront = laborRatePerHr * weeks * engineers * 40;
  const monthlyBenefit = annualBenefit / 12;
  const netMonthlyBenefit = monthlyBenefit - monthlyOverhead;
  if (netMonthlyBenefit <= 0) return Infinity;
  return Math.ceil(upfront / netMonthlyBenefit);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust for ARR vs one-time benefits?
- What metrics would you track after launch to validate forecasts?

Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design privacy-preserving telemetry with real-world trade-offs, budgeting, and rollout planning.

Key Concepts

- Differential privacy (local DP) and epsilon budgeting
- Telemetry design, sampling, data retention
- Cost modeling: client overhead, backend aggregation, storage, compliance
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

```javascript
// Example: simple local DP noise for a numeric metric
function addLaplaceNoise(x, b) {
  const u = Math.random() - 0.5;
  const noise = -b * Math.sign(u) * Math.log(1 - 2 * Math.abs(u));
  return x + noise;
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees in production and monitor budget usage?
- How would you handle drift in telemetry data affecting utility and need for budget adjustments?

